\title{The same claim with a recursor at the head: \code{\verb~|R I = R h~} is rejected officially}
\taxon{Example}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{soundness}
\tag{machine}
\meta{origin}{docs/design/review/soundness-shortcuts.md}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The first equation of [the triple](ex-OTWJ) is accepted officially only because its head is a definition with a regular hint. With the recursor itself at the head, with an abbreviation or with a theorem at the head, the official checker rejects the same true statement. Source: \src{docs/design/review/soundness-shortcuts.md}, section 4, and finding S-F1 of \src{docs/design/review/soundness-machine.md}; [the exactness session](ses-874D).}
\pre{\verb~|
-- I = And.intro True True True.intro True.intro,  h : And True True  an axiom
-- R x = And.rec (motive := fun _ => Nat) (fun _ _ => 5) x

theorem b1 : R I = R h                       -- official: reject
theorem b2 : F I = F h   -- F := fun x => R x, an abbreviation: official: reject
theorem b3 : Nat.succ (R I) = Nat.succ (R h) -- official: reject
theorem ok : G I = G h   -- G a definition with a regular hint: official: accept
~}
\ul{
\li{Officially the left side reduces to \code{\verb~|5~} before anything is compared, the right side stays stuck, and \code{\verb~|5~} against a stuck recursor is false. The arguments of two applications of one head are compared first only for a definition with a regular hint.}
\li{The machine without the shortcuts rejects all three, as the official checker does. With the option \code{\verb~|congruence~} it accepts them: \code{\verb~|I = h~} by proof irrelevance, then congruence under the head.}
\li{gruszka accepts all 14 exports of this class that the review tried; nano-lean accepts 6 of them, the ones whose head can be unfolded.}
\li{For each of the 15 statements of the class the review wrote the congruence step out as a term, \code{\verb~|Eq.rec~} over an \code{\verb~|Eq.refl~} between the two proofs, and the official checker accepts all 15. The statements are theorems; the official procedure only fails to find the equation.}
}
\p{Used by [the two shortcuts are sound in the theory](ins-T1F1).}
\p{See also: [the two proof-comparison shortcuts](design-proof-comparison-shortcuts).}
